<header><p class="st-kicker">principality · Greece and the Aegean</p><h1 class="st-title">Lordship of Leo Sgouros</h1><p class="st-meta">1198 CE – 1212 CE (approx.) · capital Nauplia</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Short-lived domain of the Greek magnate Leo Sgouros in the north-eastern Peloponnese, the chief resistance to the Frankish conquest of southern Greece.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leo-sgouros">Leo Sgouros</a> inherited power as archon of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nafplio">Nauplia</a> from his father around 1198, as Byzantine authority weakened. He seized <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/argos">Argos</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/corinth">Corinth</a>, attacked <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/athens">Athens</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/thebes">Thebes</a>, and married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eudokia-angelina">Eudokia</a>, daughter of the deposed emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexios-iii-angelos">Alexios III</a>, gaining a measure of legitimacy as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> fell to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fourth-crusade">Fourth Crusade</a> in 1204.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leo-sgouros">Sgouros</a> ruled as an independent strongman from fortresses rather than through any formal state, using force and reputed cruelty, and dominating the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argolid">Argolid</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corinthia">Corinthia</a> and the Isthmus. He tried to block <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boniface-i-marquis-of-montferrat">Boniface of Montferrat</a> at Thermopylae in 1204 but retreated to the near-impregnable citadel of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acrocorinth">Acrocorinth</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Besieged by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/franks">Franks</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leo-sgouros">Sgouros</a> died around 1208, reportedly riding his horse off the cliffs of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acrocorinth">Acrocorinth</a>. Its garrison held out until about 1210, and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lordship-of-argos-and-nauplia">Argos and Nauplia</a> until 1212, when they fell to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/principality-of-achaea">Principality of Achaea</a> and became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lordship-of-argos-and-nauplia">Lordship of Argos and Nauplia</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="principality, 1198 CE – 1212 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="65" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="54" r="3"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">principality</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Greece and the Aegean</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:83.54%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1198 CE – 1212 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>principality</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Nauplia</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Leo Sgouros</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Eastern Orthodox Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Medieval Greek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/greece">Greece</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Domain of Leo Sgouros</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1205&amp;focus=lordship-of-leo-sgouros" aria-label="Lordship of Leo Sgouros on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5250 826 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Lordship of Leo Sgouros lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5570 1082L5709 970M5570 1082L5530 1071"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5709 970h0M5530 1071h0"/><pa